     "text": "This is the final round, so I am resubmitting the round-7 configuration rather than a new variant. It is the best measured result (0.0205 ms):\n\n- **Near the bandwidth floor.** The kernel moves 120 MiB: two 40 MiB input reads and one 40 MiB output write. At the measured 6.54 TB/s peak, that takes at least about 19.2 \u00b5s if all of it reaches DRAM. The best runs are at 20.5 \u00b5s, which is about 94% of that floor.\n- **Block size and wave tail are not the limit.** BLOCK=2048 (round 9) and BLOCK=4096 timed the same. That makes block launch rate and wave quantization unlikely bottlenecks.\n- **Loads in flight are not the limit.** At either size, each SM has well over 100 KB of loads outstanding, which is more than enough.\n- **Untested alternatives are coin flips.** Other options I considered, such as `.cv`/`.cg` load modifiers or larger CTAs, could just as easily be slower. Run-to-run noise is about \u00b11.5 \u00b5s.\n\nThe one change that clearly helped was storing the output with `evict_last` and loading inputs with `evict_first`, so that is kept.\n\n```python title=\"impl_triton.py\"\nimport torch\nimport triton\nimport triton.language as tl\n\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# Fixed configuration literals\n# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# 128-thread CTAs, 32 fp16 per thread per tensor (4 x 16B vector accesses).\n# Inputs are streamed exactly once (evict_first: preferred L2 victims); the\n# output is stored with evict_last so its dirty lines stay resident in the\n# 126.5 MiB L2 rather than competing with the input reads for DRAM bandwidth\n# while the kernel runs. Full-traffic DRAM floor at the measured 6.54 TB/s is\n# ~19.2 us for 120 MiB; this configuration measured 20.5 us (best so far).\n_BLOCK = 4096\n_NUM_WARPS = 4\n_NUM_STAGES = 1\n\n_CONFIG = {\n    \"BLOCK\": _BLOCK,\n    \"num_warps\": _NUM_WARPS,\n    \"num_stages\": _NUM_STAGES,\n    \"elems_per_thread\": _BLOCK // (_NUM_WARPS * 32),\n    \"load_eviction_policy\": \"evict_first\",\n    \"store_eviction_policy\": \"evict_last\",\n    \"store_cache_modifier\": \"default\",\n}\n\n\n@triton.jit\ndef _vector_add_kernel(x_ptr, y_ptr, out_ptr, n,\n                       BLOCK: tl.constexpr, EVEN: tl.constexpr):\n    pid = tl.program_id(0)\n    offs = pid * BLOCK + tl.arange(0, BLOCK)\n    offs = tl.max_contiguous(tl.multiple_of(offs, BLOCK), BLOCK)\n    if EVEN:\n        x = tl.load(x_ptr + offs, eviction_policy=\"evict_first\")\n        y = tl.load(y_ptr + offs, eviction_policy=\"evict_first\")\n        tl.store(out_ptr + offs, x + y, eviction_policy=\"evict_last\")\n    else:\n        mask = offs < n\n        x = tl.load(x_ptr + offs, mask=mask, other=0.0,\n                    eviction_policy=\"evict_first\")\n        y = tl.load(y_ptr + offs, mask=mask, other=0.0,\n                    eviction_policy=\"evict_first\")\n        tl.store(out_ptr + offs, x + y, mask=mask,\n                 eviction_policy=\"evict_last\")\n\n\ndef run(x, y):\n    x = x.contiguous()\n    y = y.contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    n = x.numel()\n    if n == 0:\n        return out\n    grid = (triton.cdiv(n, _BLOCK),)\n    even = (n % _BLOCK) == 0\n    _vector_add_kernel[grid](\n        x, y, out, n,\n        BLOCK=_BLOCK, EVEN=even,\n        num_warps=_NUM_WARPS, num_stages=_NUM_STAGES,\n    )\n    return out\n\n\ndef get_last_config() -> dict:\n    return dict(_CONFIG)\n```",
